    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=b304847e-644d-41ca-b0f4-2f402a4a60f4&ccId=9203004009268_3&jobId=9207106806784_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Adjunct",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-01\n\nLocation: Wilmington\n\nADJUNCT INSTRUCTOR FOR PRISON EDUCATION – WILMINGTON COLLEGE SUMMARY OF POSITION: The office of Academic Affairs at Wilmington College in Wilmington, OH invites applications for adjunct faculty instructors to teach courses in our Prison Education Program, located in Warren Correctional, Lebanon Correctional and Dayton Correctional Institutions. Most classes are held in the evening between 5 and 8 pm and require a background check and in-prison training before the semester begins. We are seeking instructors qualified to teach courses in:    Math (Algebra, College Algebra, and Basic Math) Business  (Business Law, Marketing Management, Business Statistics, Introduction to Marketing, Introduction to Management) Accounting and Finance (Financial Accounting, Corporate Finance, Money and Banking) Peace Studies Other general education fields (music, visual arts, humanities, social sciences, science)    These courses are in person and require either a Master’s degree in the field of instruction or 18 graduate credit hours in the field of instruction. Classes are in person within a prison setting. Students are incarcerated at the above-mentioned facilities. Training about how to teach in a prison setting will be provided MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Candidates must have a Master’s degree or at least 18 graduate credit hours in the field of instruction.  APPLICATION DEADLINE DATE:  Rolling APPLICATION PROCESS: All Applicants are required to submit the following: Letter of Application Resume",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=b304847e-644d-41ca-b0f4-2f402a4a60f4&ccId=9203004009268_3&jobId=9207042411893_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Digital Content Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\n\nLocation: Wilmington\n\nThis role will support the College’s digital storytelling and production of media assets. From filming and video editing to social media creation, this role is ideal for a creative storyteller who thrives on turning raw footage and ideas into compelling content that engages our audience. Responsibilities • Work closely with leadership in PR, Communications and Marketing to support the digital content creation and overall marketing efforts in a manner consistent with the College’s marketing strategies • Plan, film, and edit video content for social media, web, and other digital platforms • Collaborate with staff, faculty and students to identify and capture stories worth telling through various digital platforms • Maintain consistent brand voice and visual style across all works • Stay current on social media trends and video production techniques Qualifications • Bachelor’s degree in Film and Media Production or a related field preferred • 1–3 years of experience in video editing • Experience in a higher education setting a plus • Proficiency with Adobe Premiere Pro as well as Adobe Photoshop or Lightroom • Experience with Adobe After Effects is a plus • Strong understanding of social media platforms (Instagram, TikTok, YouTube, LinkedIn, Facebook etc.) and best practices for each • Excellent storytelling instincts and attention to detail • A proactive, energetic approach to work, with the ability to juggle multiple projects and deadlines This position reports to the Director of Communication & Enrollment Operations",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=b304847e-644d-41ca-b0f4-2f402a4a60f4&ccId=9203004009268_3&jobId=9207042216924_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Intern",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-23\n\nLocation: Wilmington\n\nServes as an intern for Tennis team.  Performs other duties as assigned by the Head Coach or Senior Director of Athletics. Reports to: Head Tennis Coach/Senior Director of Athletics Duties and Responsibilities: Assists with Coaching Actively recruits new students from a specific assigned area. Maintains all requested charts, statistics, film breakdown, practice planning, etc. Works with Athletic Training staff concerning medical room operations, health services, exams, referrals, etc.  Assists head coach in overseeing the study table if applicable Maintains awareness of and follows all NCAA and college rules. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications Related Bachelor's degree, plus any related coaching experience or equivalent. Evidence of excellent coaching skills and demonstrated organizational ability to recruit student-athletes and implement a competitive football program. Ability to quickly build rapport and to communicate effectively with a diverse population",
      "department": ""
