    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=b304847e-644d-41ca-b0f4-2f402a4a60f4&ccId=9203004009268_3&jobId=9206978785608_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Campus Safety Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-16\n\nLocation: Wilmington\n\nPosition Summary :  Ensures the safety of faculty, staff, and students and monitors facilities, ensuring compliance with college rules and dealing with emergency situations. THIS IS A WEEKEND SHIFT POSITION- PART TIME  (12 hour shift)  Duties and Responsibilities:  (*Indicates non-essential function)   Patrols campus during nighttime hours, checks boilers and other equipment for proper operation and reports unusual situations.  Provides escorts on campus as needed. Checks outside windows in dorms and windows and doors in all campus buildings, including Greek houses, the Campus Village, Fife Avenue, and College Commons.  Deals with students or other persons on campus who are in violation of college rules in a reasonable but effective manner. Exercises judgement and contacts proper authorities when situation warrants. Answers radio/telephone for emergency calls as needed, including weekends and holidays. Performs routine maintenance assistance and servicing of institutional vehicles.  Periodically assists custodial staff where needed. Serves as an on-call person to help cover special events.  Assists in covering for absence of other officers. Attends department meeting and special training programs outside normal work schedule. Periodically checks all parking lots to ensure that vehicles are safe.   Checks for illegally parked vehicles and issues tickets or has them removed. Locks and unlocks buildings as scheduled.  Performs related duties as needed or as assigned. Performance Standards:   Performs assigned responsibilities in an accurate, timely and effective manner with minimal supervision and meets established timelines for special assignments. Exhibits requisite skills and knowledge and an appreciation for confidentiality.   Makes positive contributions to effective teamwork within the work unit and with other college departments. Strives for excellence in performance of responsibilities and in meeting needs of clients/students served. Knows and observes college and departmental policies, guidelines and procedures. Qualifications:   High school diploma or equivalent.  Specialized training in safety and security plus at least six months of security experience highly desirable.   Possession of an Ohio driver’s license. Evidence of a high degree of maturity and dependability, with the ability to make sound judgements and deal with emergency situations. Ability to communicate effectively with a broad range of individuals who may require persuasion or other appropriate action.  Ability to write reports and maintain records and logs. Background in investigations helpful. Willingness to independently work night shifts.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=b304847e-644d-41ca-b0f4-2f402a4a60f4&ccId=9203004009268_3&jobId=9206977892860_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Asst Professor Biology",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-15\n\nLocation: Wilmington\n\nWilmington College is a career-oriented liberal arts institution founded by and closely affiliated with the Religious Society of Friends (Quakers). Our beautiful main campus is located in southwestern Ohio. We encourage you to review our website and learn about our history, what we are doing today and how we are preparing for tomorrow. It is an exciting time here at Wilmington College. The Department of Biology at Wilmington College is seeking a broadly trained biologist who complements existing faculty expertise. This is a full time, 9-month, tenure track position as Assistant Professor of Biology, beginning January 2027. We are seeking candidates who will work collegially and effectively with faculty, students, staff, administrative colleagues, and alumni. The successful candidate will teach lecture and laboratory sections of the freshman biology sequence as well as upper division courses in Molecular Biology, Biochemistry, Microbiology and an upper-level course in their area of expertise that complements the existing curriculum. The candidate will serve as a research mentor for undergraduate capstone research projects. Qualifications: · Ph.D. required · Experience in and enthusiasm for teaching biology at the college level. · Familiarity with the small college environment preferred. · Strong interpersonal skills. To apply, submit a letter of interest, current CV, statement of teaching philosophy, copy of unofficial transcripts, and the names and contact information of at least three professional references. Wilmington College is an equal opportunity employer and will not discriminate unlawfully in employment matters on the basis of race, religion, gender, color, ancestry, national origin, age, disability or any other category protected by law. Wilmington College offers a competitive compensation package including group medical, dental, vision, life and disability, retirement plan, paid holidays, vacation and sick days. We also offer tuition remission benefits, free admission to athletic and theatrical events, and discounted meals and bookstore items. Wilmington College conducts background investigations including criminal, work history and credential confirmation on all employees as a condition of continued employment. Some positions may require additional motor vehicle record review and drug screening. Must be able to provide documentation for proof of eligibility to work in the United States. Review of applications will begin immediately and remain open until the position is filled.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=b304847e-644d-41ca-b0f4-2f402a4a60f4&ccId=9203004009268_3&jobId=9206916068095_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Prison Site Facilitator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-09-09\n\nLocation: Wilmington\n\nPART-TIME SITE FACILITATOR FOR PRISON EDUCATION – WILMINGTON COLLEGE SUMMARY OF POSITION: The office of Academic Affairs at Wilmington College in Wilmington, OH invites applications for part-time, hourly site facilitators for prison education to begin as soon as possible. A site facilitator is responsible for being present during class hours (mostly 5-8 pm Monday-Thursday, with limited daytime hours) at Warren Correctional Institution, Lebanon Correctional Institution, and/or Dayton Correctional Institution. The successful applicant will be expected to aid faculty and students in opening the college office and classrooms, putting in student passes, entering student attendance, making copies for faculty, and ensuring that class time runs smoothly. This position is hourly and part time. Number of hours per week and locations is negotiable, based on institutional and applicant need. Additional hours may be available in future semesters. The applicant will need to pass a background check and participate in required training with the Ohio Department of Rehabilitation and Correction to enter our prison sites. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: The successful candidate will have strong interpersonal and organizational skills and demonstrate a commitment to higher education opportunities for incarcerated individuals.  APPLICATION DEADLINE DATE:  Applications will be considered on a rolling basis. APPLICATION PROCESS: All Applicants are required to submit the following: Resume Names and contact information for at least 3 professional references",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=b304847e-644d-41ca-b0f4-2f402a4a60f4&ccId=9203004009268_3&jobId=9206790860142_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Director Housing and Residence Life",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-24\n\nLocation: Wilmington\n\nPosition Summary  The Director of Housing & Residence Life provides strategic leadership, vision, and oversight for a comprehensive portfolio of student life programs and services that promote student belonging, leadership development, residential engagement, and holistic student success. Reporting to the VP, Chief Student Affairs Officer/Dean of Students, the Director serves as a key member of the Student Affairs leadership team and works collaboratively across the institution to create an inclusive, engaging, and supportive campus environment.  The Director provides leadership for Housing and Residence Life. The position is responsible for developing and implementing programs, policies, and services that enhance the student experience while advancing institutional mission, values, retention, persistence, and student success goals.  The Director supervises professional and student staff, manages departmental budgets, oversees residential operations, responds to student concerns and crises, and collaborates with campus and external partners to support a vibrant and values-based campus community.  Key Responsibilities  Housing and Residence Life  • Provide strategic and operational leadership for Housing and Residence Life, ensuring the productive, effective, and student-centered operation of residential facilities and programs.  • Supervise the selection, training, evaluation, development, and discipline of professional and undergraduate residence life staff.  • Oversee residence hall programming and initiatives that foster community, belonging, and student development.  • Supervise the room selection, housing assignment, and lottery processes and ensure effective implementation of housing policies and procedures.  • Interpret and enforce housing policies, procedures, and community standards while balancing institutional expectations with student support and developmental needs.  • Oversee housing and meal plan accounts, meal plan exemptions, room condition reports, damage assessments, and related processes.  • Develop and maintain policies, procedures, publications, and communications necessary for the efficient operation of residential life.  • Coordinate with Physical Plant, Campus Safety, Dining Services, Information Technology, and other campus partners regarding residential facilities, maintenance, safety, technology, and operational needs.  • Develop and implement plans for residential facility improvements and participate in the selection, purchasing, repair, and maintenance of residence hall furnishings and equipment.  • Coordinate summer housing and conference use of residential facilities and assist with institutional programs and events such as orientation, Host Days, Family Day, registration, and other special events.  • Recruit, select, supervise, train, evaluate, and develop professional staff, graduate assistants, undergraduate staff, student employees, and administrative support personnel within the assigned areas.  • Develop, manage, and monitor budgets for Housing and Residence Life, student engagement, fraternity and sorority life, residential programming, and related initiatives.  • Oversee applicable student organization and residential programming funds and ensure appropriate review, approval, documentation, and fiscal accountability.  • Lead departmental strategic planning, program assessment, learning outcome development, and annual reporting.  • Establish and utilize assessment practices to evaluate student learning, engagement, satisfaction, retention, and program effectiveness.  • Represent Student Affairs on institutional committees, task forces, working groups, and professional organizations.  • Develop collaborative relationships with faculty, staff, students, alumni, parents and families, community partners, and external organizations.  • Serve as part of the on-call and crisis response structure for Housing and Residence Life and respond appropriately to residential emergencies and student concerns.  Student Support, Conduct, and Crisis Response  • Provide support and referrals to students experiencing academic, personal, behavioral, or other concerns, connecting students with appropriate campus and community resources.  • Serve as a judicial or conduct advisor as assigned and participate in student conduct processes.  • Respond to student emergencies and crisis situations with sound judgment, flexibility, and appropriate follow-through.  • Collaborate with Counseling, Academic Affairs, Campus Safety, Athletics, Health Services, and other campus partners to address complex student needs.  • Promote practices that support student well-being, persistence, belonging, and successful integration into the campus community.  Qualifications  Required  • Master's degree in relevant fields of Higher Education Administration, Educational Leadership, Student Personnel or other relevant fields. This can also be made up for by relevant experience.  • At least three to five years of progressively responsible professional experience in student affairs, student housing/residence life, or related areas.  • Demonstrated experience supervising professional and student staff.  • Demonstrated knowledge of student development, leadership education, and residential life.  • Experience with budget development, fiscal management, and operational planning.  • Demonstrated ability to advise, mentor, and support a diverse student population.  • Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, organizational, and problem-solving skills.  • Demonstrated ability to respond effectively and appropriately to student concerns, emergencies, and crisis situations.  • Ability to work collaboratively across departments and build effective relationships with students, faculty, staff, families, alumni, and external partners.  • Willingness and ability to work evenings and weekends and participate in an on-call or emergency response rotation as required.  Preferred  • Experience with strategic planning, program assessment, learning outcomes, and data-informed decision-making.  • Experience with residential facilities management, housing assignments, room selection processes, and residential operations.  • Experience with StarRez Student Housing Management Software.  • Professional involvement with organizations such as NASPA, ACPA, ACUHO-I, or related professional associations.  Core Competencies  • Student-Centered Leadership: Demonstrates a commitment to student development, belonging, persistence, well-being, and success.  • Strategic Leadership: Translates institutional mission and strategic priorities into effective student affairs programs, policies, and services.  • Relationship Building: Builds trust and productive partnerships with students, faculty, staff, families, alumni, and external organizations.  • Staff Development: Effectively recruits, supervises, evaluates, mentors, and develops professional and student employees.  • Crisis Management and Judgment: Responds calmly and effectively to complex student, residential, behavioral, and emergency situations.  • Organizational and Operational Management: Demonstrates strong planning, prioritization, project management, and attention to detail.  • Fiscal Responsibility: Effectively develops, monitors, and manages departmental and program budgets.  • Inclusive Leadership: Creates environments that respect and support students and colleagues from diverse backgrounds and experiences.  • Collaboration: Works effectively across institutional divisions and functional areas to advance student success.  • Assessment and Continuous Improvement: Uses data, assessment, and student feedback to evaluate programs and improve services.  • Mission Alignment: Demonstrates commitment to the institution's mission, values, and purpose.  Working Conditions  This position requires flexibility to work outside of traditional business hours, including evenings and weekends, based on student programs, residence life needs, campus events, and emergency situations. The Director will participate in the Student Affairs/Housing and Residence Life on-call structure as assigned and may be required to respond to urgent residential or student concerns.  The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to balance strategic leadership with hands-on operational oversight while maintaining a visible, accessible, and student-centered presence across campus",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=b304847e-644d-41ca-b0f4-2f402a4a60f4&ccId=9203004009268_3&jobId=9206731512798_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Admissions Counselor",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-08-19\n\nLocation: Wilmington\n\nBasic Function:   Admission Counselor:  Responsible for leading prospective students through the admission, financial aid, and registration processes to matriculate at Wilmington College. Tasks include, but are not limited to, traveling to high schools, attending college fairs, recruiting events on and off campus (including some overnight stays), processing admission files, communicating with perspective students and families, visiting with prospective students and their families, providing campus tours. An admission counselor at Wilmington College is charged with effectively managing a recruitment territory and meeting institutional enrollment goals.  Duties and Responsibilities Provide effective and professional customer service to prospective students and their families. Visit with prospective students (and their families) to provide a welcoming and thorough overview of the opportunities available at Wilmington College Provide correspondence to prospective students through all channels of communication including phone, text, email, and parent outreach. Develop innovative recruitment strategies and execute those strategies in a collaborative and team building environment. Visit, develop, and maintain strong working relationships with high school educators, guidance professionals and access organization leaders. Represent Wilmington College enthusiastically at various college fairs and events.  Attend on and off-campus planned admission recruiting events and programs. Assume secondary planning and implementation responsibility for recruitment territory events on and off-campus. Utilize integrated database to process admission files, award scholarship and communicate effectively with prospective students. Conduct financial aid counseling contacts with students including the verification process and financial aid award review. Actively attend and contribute to weekly Admission staff meetings. Perform other duties as assigned by the Director of Admission and/or Associate Director of Admission and/or Vice President of Enrollment.   Performance Standards: Meets objectives in a timely and effective manner as outlined in the office policies and procedures documents and strives to fulfill objectives and the college's strategic agenda. Exhibits necessary level of knowledge and expertise and effectively interfaces with prospective students, their families, the WC campus, and with the admission team. Serves as an effective and positive-thinking team member and coordinates professionally with other college departments/employees. Strives for excellence in performance of responsibilities, meeting needs of prospective students/families, and building professional relationships with the enrollment team. Maintains professional and timely follow-up in all admission and financial aid processes. Exhibits a commitment to being a dedicated member of the College community and enrollment team. Maintains a consistent professional appearance and positive outlook. Conduct is professional and meets office policy standards. Enthusiastically knows and observes college and departmental policies, guidelines, and procedures.     Qualifications: Bachelor's Degree: experience working in Higher Education is preferred. Experience with diversity outreach and college access in secondary or higher education. Evidence of excellent communication and presentation skills, with ability to communicate effectively across cultures with a diverse population. Demonstrates organizational ability, effective time-management skills, and ability to prioritize in a multi-task work environment. Demonstrates and enjoys collegial interactions with the public and co-workers.  Good computer skills with background using Microsoft Office, web applications and database experience is preferred. Possession of or ability to obtain a valid Ohio driver’s license and willingness to travel for recruitment events. Familiarity with private higher education admission and/or financial aid is preferred. Willingness to work evenings and weekends as schedule and work-load dictates.",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=b304847e-644d-41ca-b0f4-2f402a4a60f4&ccId=9203004009268_3&jobId=9205713313155_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "International Student Liaison & Community Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-04-14\n\nLocation: Wilmington\n\nInternational Student Liaison & Community Coordinator Reports To Director of International Affairs Position Summary The International Student Liaison & Community Coordinator plays a vital role in enhancing the well-being, engagement, and integration of international students at Wilmington College. This position is responsible for developing and managing programs that foster a sense of belonging, provide meaningful support, and connect international students with the campus and local Wilmington community. A secondary function includes providing administrative support to the international admissions process under the close guidance of the Director. The ideal candidate has a passion for cross-cultural community building, student success, and the mission of the college. Key Responsibilities A. Student Support & Community Integration (Primary Focus) Serve as the primary non-academic point of contact for enrolled international students, providing guidance and referral to campus resources. Develop, launch, and manage the International Host Family Program, including recruiting, screening, and training local community members, and matching them with students. Plan and execute comprehensive orientation and ongoing cultural transition programs for new and returning international students. Organize regular cultural, social, and educational events to promote community building and cross-cultural exchange. Create and disseminate digital and print resources (e.g., welcome guides, monthly newsletters, community event calendars) to support student adjustment. B. Admissions & Recruitment Support (Under Supervision) Assist the Director with the initial stages of the international application process, including document collection and initial communication with applicants. Help maintain accurate applicant records within the office's management system. Contribute to the creation of engaging student testimonials and promotional content for recruitment purposes, utilizing digital media skills. Represent the Office of International Affairs at select on-campus recruitment and yield events. C. Digital Communications & Social Media Management Develop and manage the social media strategy and presence for the Office of International Affairs across relevant platforms (e.g., Instagram, Facebook, snapchat). Create and schedule regular, engaging content—including photos, videos, student spotlights, event promotions, and informational posts—that highlight the international student experience and supports office initiatives. Monitor engagement, respond to messages, and analyze metrics to refine digital outreach effectiveness. D. Campus & Community Collaboration Collaborate closely with key campus partners, including Student Life, Campus Ministry, Residence Life, and Academic Departments, to ensure a coordinated support network. Build and maintain relationships with local community organizations, businesses, and faith groups to develop opportunities for student engagement and support. Serve as an advocate for international student needs in relevant campus meetings. Qualifications Required Bachelor's degree. Exceptional interpersonal, verbal, and written communication skills. Demonstrated experience in program planning, event coordination, or community outreach. Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple projects simultaneously. High degree of cultural sensitivity and a commitment to fostering an inclusive environment. Commitment to the mission and culture of Wilmington College. Preferred Degree or significant coursework in Communication Arts, Digital Media, International Studies, or a related field. Personal experience living, studying, or working in an intercultural environment. Skills in digital content creation (e.g., Adobe Suite, Final Cut, social media management). Basic understanding of F-1 student regulations (training will be provided).",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
